cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use crate, please cite it by its DOI, 10.5281/zenodo.23289273.
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'crate: Canonical Schemas for Changing Data and Provenance Receipts'
version: 0.16.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23289273
abstract: 'Declares a canonical shape for each file or table it registers, reads a
  registered file to that shape whichever known layout arrives, and holds data read
  some other way to the same shape, so a change in a registered file''s columns or
  layout is fixed once in crate rather than in every reader downstream. Also holds
  the provenance receipt contract: a JSON Schema, RFC 8785 canonical JSON, a table
  fingerprint and test vectors, with R functions that write receipts and compare two
  builds as identical, equivalent within a declared tolerance, or different. Under
  active development.'
